# Documentation Standards

## When to Update Docs
- New or changed HTTP endpoint (routes, handlers, DTOs, status codes)
- Auth / RBAC role or Keycloak behavior changes
- OpenTelemetry / observability config changes
- New env vars in `internal/config/`
- Database schema changes (`cmd/migrations/sql/`)

## What to Document

### OpenAPI (required for `/api/v1` HTTP changes)
- swag annotations on handlers + `cmd/server/main.go` metadata (`@BasePath /api/v1`)
- Regenerate: `make swagger-load`
- Commit `docs/swagger.yaml`, `docs/swagger.json`, and `docs/docs.go` together

### Feature / ops docs (when behavior changes)

| Doc | Update when |
|-----|-------------|
| `docs/RBAC_GUIDE.md` / `docs/RBAC_QUICK_START.md` | Roles, permissions, `RequireRole` usage |
| `docs/KEYCLOAK_RBAC_SETUP.md` | Keycloak realm/client/role mapping |
| `docs/OPENTELEMETRY.md` | OTel exporter, collector, Jaeger, env vars |

### Human docs
- `README.md` — setup, `make` targets
- `CONTRIBUTING.md` — contribution expectations
- `cmd/server/.env.example` — new required env vars (no secrets)

## Style
- Concise and practical — include real `make` / `curl` examples with `/api/v1` path prefix
- Verify paths and commands exist in this repo
- Outdated docs are worse than no docs
